#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch's algorithm"
msgstr "El algoritmo de Deutsch"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves the parity problem for the special case that $n = 1.$\n"
"In the context of quantum computing this problem is sometimes referred to as *Deutsch's problem*, and we'll follow that nomenclature in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo de Deutsch resuelve el problema de la paridad para el caso especial en que $n = 1.$\n"
"En el contexto de la computación cuántica, este problema a veces se denomina *problema de Deutsch*, y seguiremos esa nomenclatura en esta lección.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, the input is represented by a function $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ from one bit to one bit.\n"
"There are four such functions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ser precisos, la entrada se representa mediante una función $f:\\Sigma \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ de un bit a un bit.\n"
"Existen cuatro funciones de este tipo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rule[-10mm]{0mm}{10mm}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_1(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_2(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 0\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_3(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & f_4(a)\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first and last of these functions are *constant* and the middle two are *balanced*, meaning that the two possible output values for the function occur the same number of times as we range over the inputs.\n"
"Deutsch's problem is to determine which of these two categories the input function belongs to: constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"La primera y la última de estas funciones son *constantes*, mientras que las dos del medio son *balanceadas*, lo que significa que los dos posibles valores de salida de la función aparecen el mismo número de veces al recorrer las entradas.\n"
"El problema de Deutsch consiste en determinar a cuál de estas dos categorías pertenece la función de entrada: constante o balanceada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch's problem\">\n"
"Input:  a function $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"El problema de Deutsch\">\n"
"Entrada: una función $f:\\{0,1\\}\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Salida: $0$ si $f$ es constante, $1$ si $f$ es balanceada\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we view the input function $f$ in Deutsch's problem as representing "
"random access to a string, we're thinking about a two-bit string: "
"$f(0)f(1).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si vemos la función de entrada $f$ del problema de Deutsch como un acceso "
"aleatorio a una cadena, estamos pensando en una cadena de dos bits: "
"$f(0)f(1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"\\mathsf{function} & \\mathsf{string}\\\\\n"
"\\hline\n"
"f_1 & 00 \\\\\n"
"f_2 & 01 \\\\\n"
"f_3 & 10 \\\\\n"
"f_4 & 11\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When viewed in this way, Deutsch's problem is to compute the parity (or, "
"equivalently, the exclusive-OR) of the two bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Visto de esta manera, el problema de Deutsch consiste en calcular la paridad"
" (o, de forma equivalente, el OR exclusivo) de los dos bits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every classical query algorithm that correctly solves this problem must query both bits: $f(0)$ and $f(1).$\n"
"If we learn that $f(1) = 1,$ for instance, the answer could still be $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether $f(0) = 1$ or $f(0) = 0,$ respectively.\n"
"Every other case is similar; knowing just one of two bits doesn't provide any information at all about their parity.\n"
"So, the Boolean circuit described in the previous section is the best we can do in terms of the number of queries required to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Todo algoritmo de consulta clásico que resuelva correctamente este problema debe consultar ambos bits: $f(0)$ y $f(1).$\n"
"Si aprendemos que $f(1) = 1,$ por ejemplo, la respuesta podría seguir siendo $0$ o $1$, dependiendo de si $f(0) = 1$ o $f(0) = 0$, respectivamente.\n"
"Todos los demás casos son similares; conocer solo uno de los dos bits no proporciona ninguna información sobre su paridad.\n"
"Por lo tanto, el circuito booleano descrito en la sección anterior es lo mejor que podemos hacer en términos del número de consultas necesarias para resolver este problema.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuit description {#quantum-circuit-description}"
msgstr "Descripción del circuito cuántico {#quantum-circuit-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm solves Deutsch's problem using a single query, therefore providing a quantifiable advantage of quantum over classical computations.\n"
"This may be a modest advantage — one query as opposed to two — but we have to start somewhere.\n"
"Scientific advances sometimes have seemingly humble origins.\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo de Deutsch resuelve el problema de Deutsch con una sola consulta, lo que proporciona una ventaja cuantificable de la computación cuántica sobre la clásica.\n"
"Puede parecer una ventaja modesta —una consulta en vez de dos— pero hay que empezar por algún sitio.\n"
"Los avances científicos a veces tienen orígenes aparentemente humildes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit that describes Deutsch's algorithm:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí se muestra un circuito cuántico que describe el algoritmo de Deutsch:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![El algoritmo de Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Análisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze Deutsch's algorithm, we will trace through the action of the "
"circuit above and identify the states of the qubits at the times suggested "
"by this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para analizar el algoritmo de Deutsch, recorreremos la acción del circuito "
"anterior e identificaremos los estados de los qubits en los momentos "
"indicados por esta figura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![States during Deutsch's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Estados durante el algoritmo de "
"Deutsch](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-circuit-states.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The initial state is $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle,$ and the two "
"Hadamard operations on the left-hand side of the circuit transform this "
"state to\n"
msgstr ""
"El estado inicial es $\\vert 1\\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle,$ y las dos "
"operaciones Hadamard en el lado izquierdo del circuito transforman este "
"estado en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_1 \\rangle = \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(As always, we're following Qiskit's qubit ordering convention, which puts "
"the top qubit to the right and the bottom qubit to the left.) It may feel "
"unintuitive to write this product state partly distributed (leaving the "
"states of qubit 1 factored out), but this will make our later expressions "
"more compact.\n"
msgstr ""
"(Como siempre, seguimos la convención de ordenamiento de qubits de Qiskit, "
"que coloca el qubit superior a la derecha y el qubit inferior a la "
"izquierda.) Puede resultar poco intuitivo escribir este estado producto "
"parcialmente distribuido (dejando los estados del qubit 1 factorizados), "
"pero esto hará que nuestras expresiones posteriores sean más compactas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"According to the definition of the $U_f$ gate, the value of the function $f$ for the classical state of the top/rightmost qubit is XORed onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, which transforms $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ into the state\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, se aplica la compuerta $U_f$.\n"
"De acuerdo con la definición de la compuerta $U_f$, el valor de la función $f$ para el estado clásico del qubit superior/más a la derecha se aplica con XOR al qubit inferior/más a la izquierda, lo que transforma $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ en el estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(0) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus f(1) \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can simplify this expression by observing that the formula\n"
msgstr "Podemos simplificar esta expresión observando que la fórmula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus a\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus a\\rangle = (-1)^a \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"works for both possible values $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"More explicitly, the two cases are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"es válida para ambos valores posibles $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"Más explícitamente, los dos casos son los siguientes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 0\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 0\\rangle\n"
"& = \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^0 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"\\vert 0 \\oplus 1\\rangle - \\vert 1 \\oplus 1\\rangle & = \\vert 1 \\rangle - \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^1 \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle - \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we can alternatively express $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Así, podemos expresar $\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$ de forma alternativa de la "
"siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(0)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 0 \\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{1}{2} (-1)^{f(1)} \\bigl( \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert 1 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Something interesting just happened!\n"
"Although the action of the $U_f$ gate on standard basis states leaves the top/rightmost qubit alone and XORs the function value onto the bottom/leftmost qubit, here we see that the state of the top/rightmost qubit has changed (in general) while the state of the bottom/leftmost qubit remains the same — specifically being in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state before and after the $U_f$ gate is performed.\n"
"This phenomenon is known as the *phase kickback*, and we will have more to say about it shortly.\n"
msgstr ""
"¡Algo interesante acaba de ocurrir!\n"
"Aunque la acción de la compuerta $U_f$ sobre los estados de la base estándar deja intacto el qubit superior/más a la derecha y aplica el XOR del valor de la función al qubit inferior/más a la izquierda, aquí vemos que el estado del qubit superior/más a la derecha ha cambiado (en general) mientras que el estado del qubit inferior/más a la izquierda permanece igual, estando específicamente en el estado $\\vert - \\rangle$ antes y después de que se aplique la compuerta $U_f$.\n"
"Este fenómeno se conoce como *phase kickback* (retroceso de fase), y hablaremos más sobre él en breve.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With one final simplification, which is to pull the factor of $(-1)^{f(0)}$ "
"outside of the sum, we obtain this expression of the state "
"$\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Con una última simplificación, que consiste en extraer el factor "
"$(-1)^{f(0)}$ fuera de la suma, obtenemos esta expresión del estado "
"$\\vert\\pi_2\\rangle$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\pi_2\\rangle\n"
"  & = (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"      \\biggl( \\frac{\\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(0) \\oplus f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"        (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert - \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$}.\n"
"      \\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that in this expression, we have $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ in the exponent of $-1$ as opposed to $f(1) - f(0),$ which is what we might expect from a purely algebraic viewpoint, but we obtain the same result either way.\n"
"This is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que en esta expresión tenemos $f(0) \\oplus f(1)$ en el exponente de $-1$ en lugar de $f(1) - f(0),$ que es lo que podríamos esperar desde un punto de vista puramente algebraico, pero obtenemos el mismo resultado de cualquier forma.\n"
"Esto se debe a que el valor $(-1)^k$ para cualquier entero $k$ depende únicamente de si $k$ es par o impar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying the final Hadamard gate to the top qubit leaves us with the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Aplicar la compuerta Hadamard final al qubit superior nos deja con el "
"estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\pi_3 \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 0$}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  (-1)^{f(0)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1 \\rangle & \\text{if $f(0) \\oplus f(1) = 1$},\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which leads to the correct outcome with probability $1$ when the "
"right/topmost qubit is measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"lo que conduce al resultado correcto con probabilidad $1$ cuando se mide el "
"qubit de la derecha/superior.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Further remarks on the phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-phase-"
"kickback}"
msgstr ""
"Observaciones adicionales sobre el phase kickback {#further-remarks-on-the-"
"phase-kickback}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before moving on, let's look at the analysis above from a slightly different"
" angle that may shed some light on the phase kickback phenomenon.\n"
msgstr ""
"Antes de continuar, veamos el análisis anterior desde un ángulo ligeramente "
"diferente que puede arrojar luz sobre el fenómeno del phase kickback.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, notice that the following formula works for all choices of bits "
"$b,c\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, observa que la siguiente fórmula es válida para toda elección de "
"bits $b,c\\in\\Sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus c\\rangle = X^c \\vert b \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be verified by checking it for the two possible values $c = 0$ and "
"$c = 1$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto puede verificarse comprobándolo para los dos valores posibles $c = 0$ y"
" $c = 1$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 0 \\rangle & = \\vert b\\rangle = \\mathbb{I} \\vert b \\rangle = X^0 \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert b \\oplus 1 \\rangle & = \\vert \\neg b\\rangle = X \\vert b \\rangle = X^1 \\vert b \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using this formula, we see that\n"
msgstr "Usando esta fórmula, vemos que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl(\\vert b\\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert b \\oplus f(a) \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert b \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every choice of bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"Because this formula is true for $b=0$ and $b=1,$ we see by linearity that\n"
msgstr ""
"para toda elección de bits $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"Como esta fórmula es válida para $b=0$ y $b=1$, vemos por linealidad que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)}\\vert \\psi \\rangle\\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all qubit state vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle,$ and therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"para todos los vectores de estado de qubit $\\vert \\psi\\rangle,$ y por lo "
"tanto\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle \\bigr) = \\bigl(X^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\bigr) \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= (-1)^{f(a)} \\vert - \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key that makes this work is that $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle.$\n"
"In mathematical terms, the vector $\\vert - \\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* of the matrix $X$ having *eigenvalue* $-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"La clave que hace que esto funcione es que $X\\vert - \\rangle = - \\vert - \\rangle.$\n"
"En términos matemáticos, el vector $\\vert - \\rangle$ es un *vector propio* de la matriz $X$ con *valor propio* $-1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll discuss eigenvectors and eigenvalues in greater detail in the upcoming"
" lesson on *Phase estimation and factoring,* where the phase kickback "
"phenomenon is generalized to other unitary operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Discutiremos los vectores propios y valores propios con mayor detalle en la "
"próxima lección sobre *Estimación de fase y factorización*, donde el "
"fenómeno del phase kickback se generaliza a otras operaciones unitarias.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keeping in mind that scalars float freely through tensor products, we find "
"an alternative way of reasoning how the operation $U_f$ transforms $\\vert "
"\\pi_1\\rangle$ into $\\vert \\pi_2\\rangle$ in the analysis above:\n"
msgstr ""
"Teniendo en cuenta que los escalares se propagan libremente a través de los "
"productos tensoriales, encontramos una forma alternativa de razonar cómo la "
"operación $U_f$ transforma $\\vert \\pi_1\\rangle$ en $\\vert "
"\\pi_2\\rangle$ en el análisis anterior:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\pi_2 \\rangle\n"
"  & = U_f \\bigl( \\vert - \\rangle \\vert + \\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 0\\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"    + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} U_f \\bigl(\\vert - \\rangle \\vert 1\\rangle \\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\vert - \\rangle \\biggl( \\frac{(-1)^{f(0)} \\vert 0\\rangle + (-1)^{f(1)} \\vert 1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}\\biggr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation in Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"
msgstr "Implementación en Qiskit {#implementation-in-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how we can implement Deutsch's algorithm in Qiskit. We'll start with a version check and then perform the imports required solely for this implementation.\n"
"For the implementations of other algorithms that follows, we'll perform the required imports separately for the sake of greater modularity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora veamos cómo podemos implementar el algoritmo de Deutsch en Qiskit. Comenzaremos con una verificación de versión y luego realizaremos las importaciones necesarias únicamente para esta implementación.\n"
"Para las implementaciones de otros algoritmos que siguen, realizaremos las importaciones necesarias por separado en aras de una mayor modularidad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll define a quantum circuit that implements a query gate for one of the four functions $f_1,$ $f_2,$ $f_3,$ or $f_4$ from one bit to one bit described previously. As we already mentioned, the implementation of query gates is not really a part of Deutsch's algorithm itself;\n"
"here we're essentially just showing one way to prepare the input, in the form of a circuit implementation of a query gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero definiremos un circuito cuántico que implemente una compuerta de consulta para una de las cuatro funciones $f_1,$ $f_2,$ $f_3,$ o $f_4$ de un bit a un bit descritas anteriormente. Como ya mencionamos, la implementación de las compuertas de consulta no es realmente parte del propio algoritmo de Deutsch;\n"
"aquí esencialmente solo mostramos una forma de preparar la entrada, en la forma de una implementación en circuito de una compuerta de consulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see what each circuit looks like using the `draw` method. Here's the "
"circuit for the function $f_3.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos ver cómo luce cada circuito usando el método `draw`. Aquí está el "
"circuito para la función $f_3.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-"
"outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código "
"anterior](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-"
"outputs/787e3c81-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will create the actual quantum circuit for Deutsch's algorithm, substituting the query gate with a quantum circuit implementation given as an argument. Shortly we'll plug in one of the four circuits defined by the function `deutsch_function` we defined earlier.\n"
"Barriers are included to show the visual separation between the query gate implementation and the rest of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación crearemos el circuito cuántico real para el algoritmo de Deutsch, sustituyendo la compuerta de consulta por una implementación en circuito cuántico dada como argumento. En breve conectaremos uno de los cuatro circuitos definidos por la función `deutsch_function` que definimos antes.\n"
"Se incluyen barreras para mostrar la separación visual entre la implementación de la compuerta de consulta y el resto del circuito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Again we can see what the circuit looks like using the `draw` method.\n"
msgstr "De nuevo podemos ver cómo luce el circuito usando el método `draw`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-"
"outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código "
"anterior](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-algorithm/extracted-"
"outputs/27b41067-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we'll create a function that runs the circuit previously defined "
"one time and outputs the appropriate result: \"constant\" or \"balanced.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Finalmente, crearemos una función que ejecute el circuito definido "
"anteriormente una sola vez y devuelva el resultado apropiado: \"constant\" o"
" \"balanced.\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now run Deutsch's algorithm on any one of the four functions defined "
"above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos ejecutar el algoritmo de Deutsch en cualquiera de las cuatro "
"funciones definidas anteriormente.\n"
